{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-4-6", "id": "msg_vrtx_01MH39wSGWJ3Ud4ogpN7wGFz", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Baseline evaluation complete. The skill scores 2/10 applicable patterns as \"strong\" (20%). Preparing the enhanced version now.\n\n### Steps Executed\n- Step 1: Input Handling \u2014 completed (`target-skill/SKILL.md`, valid frontmatter with `name` and `description`)\n- Step 2: Load Knowledge \u2014 completed (14 patterns loaded)\n- Step 3: Baseline Evaluation \u2014 completed, 2/10 strong (20%)\n- Step 4: Already-Optimal Detection \u2014 not optimal, continued\n- Step 5: Enhancement Targeting \u2014 completed, 8 patterns targeted (5 absent, 3 present)\n- Step 6: Rewrite \u2014 completed\n- Step 7: File Splitting \u2014 skipped (under 500 lines)\n- Step 8: Prompt Plugin Delegation \u2014 skipped (plugin not available)\n- Step 9: Changelog \u2014 in progress\n\n## Enhanced Skill\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: \"docs:changelog\"\ndescription: \"Generate a changelog entry from recent git commits. Use when preparing a release, documenting what changed between versions, or summarizing commit history into grouped categories. Do NOT use for writing narrative release notes, generating commit messages, or comparing branches without release context.\"\nargument-hint: \"<from-tag> [<to-tag>]\"\nuser-invocable: true\n---\n\n# Changelog Generator\n\nGenerate a formatted changelog entry from git commit history between two tags.\n\n## Steps\n\n### Step 1: Determine Range\n\nParse the arguments: `from-tag` is required, `to-tag` defaults to `HEAD` if omitted.\n\nVerify both refs exist before proceeding, so later steps don't produce confusing empty output:\n\n```bash\ngit rev-parse --verify ${from_tag} >/dev/null 2>&1\n```\n\nIf either ref is invalid, report: \"**Error**: Tag `<tag>` not found. Run `git tag -l` to see available tags.\" Stop.\n\nRetrieve the commits:\n\n```bash\ngit log ${from_tag}..${to_tag} --oneline --no-merges\n```\n\nThe `--no-merges` flag excludes merge commits because they duplicate the content of their merged commits and would create double-counted entries.\n\n**Completion check**: If git log returns no commits, report: \"No commits found between `<from_tag>` and `<to_tag>`.\" Stop.\n\n### Step 2: Categorize Commits\n\nGroup commits by type using conventional commit prefixes. These follow the Conventional Commits specification, the most widely adopted commit convention:\n\n- `feat:` -> Features\n- `fix:` -> Bug Fixes\n- `docs:` -> Documentation\n- `refactor:` -> Refactoring\n- `test:` -> Tests\n- `chore:` -> Maintenance\n\nCommits without a recognized prefix go into \"Other Changes\".\n\nStrip the prefix and scope from the commit subject for the entry text. For example, `feat(auth): add SSO login` becomes \"Add SSO login\" under Features.\n\nA common mistake is treating the scope (the parenthesized part in `feat(auth):`) as a sub-grouping level. Scopes provide context within the commit subject but should not create separate sub-sections in the changelog; they clutter the output without adding value for readers.\n\n### Step 3: Format Changelog\n\nOutput in Keep a Changelog format. This format groups changes by impact type, making the changelog scannable for users assessing upgrade risk.\n\n```markdown\n## [version] - YYYY-MM-DD\n\n### Features\n- Description (commit-hash)\n\n### Bug Fixes\n- Description (commit-hash)\n\n### Documentation\n- Description (commit-hash)\n```\n\nOmit sections that have no entries. Only include category headers for groups containing at least one commit.\n\n### Step 4: Check for Breaking Changes\n\nSearch commit messages and bodies for breaking change indicators. Both the footer format and the `!` suffix format must be checked because teams use them inconsistently:\n\n```bash\ngit log ${from_tag}..${to_tag} --grep=\"BREAKING CHANGE\" --format=\"%h %s\"\n```\n\nAlso check for the `!` suffix convention (e.g., `feat!:`, `fix(api)!:`):\n\n```bash\ngit log ${from_tag}..${to_tag} --format=\"%h %s\" | grep -E \"^[a-f0-9]+ \\w+(\\(.*\\))?!:\"\n```\n\nIf breaking changes are found, add a \"Breaking Changes\" section at the top of the changelog entry, above all other sections. Breaking changes go first because they represent the highest upgrade risk.\n\n### Step 5: Verify Completeness\n\nCount the commits from Step 1 and the categorized entries from Steps 2-4. Every commit must appear in exactly one section.\n\nIf counts do not match, re-examine uncategorized commits and assign them to the appropriate section or \"Other Changes\". If the mismatch persists after one re-check, present the output and note to the user which commits could not be categorized.\n\n## Example\n\nGiven this invocation:\n\n```\n/docs:changelog v1.2.0 v1.3.0\n```\n\nWith these commits between the tags:\n\n```\na1b2c3d feat(auth): add SSO login support\nd4e5f6g fix: resolve timeout on large uploads\nh7i8j9k chore: update CI config\nl0m1n2o feat!: change default auth provider\n```\n\nThe output:\n\n```markdown\n## [v1.3.0] - 2026-06-01\n\n### Breaking Changes\n- Change default auth provider (l0m1n2o)\n\n### Features\n- Add SSO login support (a1b2c3d)\n\n### Bug Fixes\n- Resolve timeout on large uploads (d4e5f6g)\n\n### Maintenance\n- Update CI config (h7i8j9k)\n```\n```\n\n---\n\n## What Changed\n\n| Pattern Applied | What was added/changed | Why |\n|----------------|----------------------|-----|\n| Exclusion Clause | Added \"Do NOT use for writing narrative release notes, generating commit messages, or comparing branches without release context\" to the description | Prevents false activation for adjacent tasks like release notes authoring or branch comparison |\n| Control Tuning | Added tag validation with specific error message and halt condition in Step 1; made empty-range an explicit stop condition | Git commands are rigid (exact format), error handling is rigid (exact messages), categorization rules are rigid, but scope handling uses judgment |\n| Explain-the-Why | Added rationale for `--no-merges` flag, Keep a Changelog format choice, why both breaking change formats must be checked, and why breaking changes go first | Enables correct judgment in edge cases (e.g., whether to include a merge commit) by understanding the intent behind each instruction |\n| Template Scaffold | Added complete filled example in new \"Example\" section showing 4 commits mapped to formatted output | The template in Step 3 shows structure; the example shows a realistic result including a breaking change, scope stripping, and section ordering |\n| In-Skill Examples | Added end-to-end example with invocation syntax, sample commits, and expected output | Demonstrates scope stripping (`feat(auth):` -> \"Add SSO login\"), breaking change detection via `!` suffix, and section omission |\n| Known Gotchas | Added inline gotcha in Step 2 about scope-as-subgrouping mistake | Conventional commit scopes are commonly misused as changelog sub-sections; calling this out at the categorization step prevents the error |\n| Execution Checklist | Added tag validation check, empty-range halt, and Step 5 verification with re-check and bail-out behavior | Each step now has a clear completion criterion and the workflow halts gracefully on invalid input |\n| Self-Correcting Loop | Added Step 5 with commit count verification, one retry for uncategorized commits, and user notification on persistent mismatch | Catches missed or duplicated entries before presenting the output; bail-out after one retry prevents infinite loops |\n\n## Status Change\n\n| Pattern | Before | After |\n|---------|--------|-------|\n| Exclusion Clause | absent | strong |\n| Control Tuning | present | strong |\n| Explain-the-Why | absent | strong |\n| Template Scaffold | present | strong |\n| In-Skill Examples | absent | strong |\n| Known Gotchas | absent | strong |\n| Execution Checklist | present | strong |\n| Self-Correcting Loop | absent | strong |\n\n**Summary**: 8 patterns improved (5 absent->strong, 3 present->strong), 0 new files proposed. Score moved from 2/10 strong (20%) to 10/10 strong (100%)."}], "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 125, "cache_read_input_tokens": 61625, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 125, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 2}, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "93541718-ef78-426b-8690-dd39026def46", "uuid": "828b40f2-0f13-4e42-8f8f-1f4f38560987", "request_id": "req_vrtx_011CbccxGDGy12LGHkr8A6bb", "timestamp": "2026-06-01T13:30:37.917Z"}
